# Android Roles Bootstrap

Apply this rule at the start of every Android task in this repository.

## Role activation

- Use architecture first, then domain specialists (UI, networking, data), then QA/security/accessibility checks.
- Run independent specialist tasks in parallel when possible.
- Ask for clarification before adding new dependencies or changing established project patterns.

## Source role files

Use the existing role rules in `.cursor/rules/` as detailed role definitions:

- `android-agent-orchestration.mdc`
- `android-project-arch.mdc`
- `android-ux-ui-design-agent.mdc`
- `android-concurrency-networking-agent.mdc`
- `android-persistence-specialist.mdc`
- `android-testing-qa-agent.mdc`
- `android-security-reviewer.mdc`
- `android-accessibility-specialist.mdc`
- `android-performance-optimizer.mdc`

## Matching existing stack

- Detect and follow existing architecture and libraries before implementation.
- Prefer consistency with the current codebase over introducing new approaches.
